PARITY (reproduced from the web source — composition, data, states, i18n)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Data hook  : web useIncidents({ activeOnly: true }) (GET /status/incidents?active=1) → the P1/S8 `IncidentsSource`
               read seam (push-based onUpdate + start/stop/refresh); the view performs no HTTP. The "Log incident" CTA
               mounts the sibling IncidentForm (its useCreateIncident lives there, surface 0246) via an injected
               IncidentCreating seam; the sheet's dismissal refetches the list (web create→qc.invalidate).
  Composition: header (AlertTriangle glyph + "Active incidents" + count Badge + ghost "Log incident") over the list of
               compact rows; each row = severity icon (AlertCircle/Triangle/Octagon) + title (truncate) + status Badge +
               severity label + optional "Affects: …" + "Started <rel>[· N updates]" + chevron, opening
               /system-status/incidents/:id. SEVERITY_TONE (minor=amber, major=orange, critical=red) reproduced from the
               semantic tokens (orange = perceptual mix of warning+danger). STATUS_BADGE (investigating=danger,
               identified=warning, monitoring=info, resolved=success) reproduced 1:1.
  States     : every state renders (no hidden surface). The web card returns null when there are no active incidents;
               per the P4 "every state MUST render — no hidden surfaces" mandate the native surface instead renders a
               labeled empty state and keeps the amber alarm treatment ONLY while incidents are present (a documented,
               intentional widening — the ActiveSessionsSection precedent — NOT silent drift). loading (spinner) /
               empty (friendly "all clear") / error (QueryError-style + Retry) / content, plus the inline reload-error
               over cached rows + the stale chip + auto-refresh + the offline cached banner (ADR-013). Each branch has a
               preview + a unit test + an executed host check.
  i18n keys  : every web literal shipped in the "IncidentsCard" table — "Active incidents"; "Log incident"; the severity
               labels minor/major/critical; the status labels investigating/identified/monitoring/resolved; "Affects:
               {{components}}"; "Started {{time}}"; "{{count}} updates"; the relativeFrom units (just now / {{count}}m
               ago / {{count}}h ago / {{count}}d ago). Native-only chrome (still localized): loading / empty / error /
               retry / Live·Stale·Offline / banners / a11y count + row-status. The view holds no bare English literal
               (all via the IncidentsCardStrings facade).
  Apple HIG  : SwiftUI card; native Button rows (44pt targets, .isButton trait, per-row a11y label + automation id);
               TimelineView(.periodic by:60) refreshes the relative timestamps without a model timer; ContentUnavailable
               View for empty; sheet-presented IncidentForm; Dynamic Type (token fonts), Reduce-Motion-safe motion
               (TSFadeIn/TSStagger honor the env), VoiceOver labels on every control, decorative icons hidden. iOS 18 /
               iPadOS 18 / macOS 15 all type-check (Color.mix, TimelineView, ContentUnavailableView, .sheet all resolve
               on both SDKs).

